    "text": "A paramagnetic material has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>28</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>atoms</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Its magnetic susceptibility at temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>350</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is <math><mn>2.8</mn><mo>Ã—</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Its susceptibility at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is",
